        <p class="eyebrow">Foundations</p>
        <h2>Tokens, live</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Every value below is read from <code>tokens.css</code> and <code>global.css</code> at build time.
          Swatches, bars and boxes use <code>var(--token)</code>; the name/value labels are parsed from the
          real file text. If a token changes, this page changes with it.
        </p>

        <h3>Colour</h3>
        <div class="token-grid">
          {colorTokens.map((t) => (
            <div class="token-swatch">
              <div class="color-fill" style={`background:var(${t.name})`}></div>
              <div class="token-swatch-meta">
                <code class="token-swatch-name">{t.name}</code>
                <span class="token-swatch-hex">{t.value}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <h3>Type scale</h3>
        <div class="type-samples">
          <div>
            <h1>Aa — Heading one</h1>
            <code class="atom-tag">h1 · var(--font-heading)</code>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h2>Aa — Heading two</h2>
            <code class="atom-tag">h2 · var(--font-heading)</code>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Aa — Heading three</h3>
            <code class="atom-tag">h3 · var(--font-heading)</code>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="lede">Aa — lede paragraph, the size used for section intros.</p>
            <code class="atom-tag">.lede · var(--font-body)</code>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p>Aa — body paragraph, the default reading size and weight for prose.</p>
            <code class="atom-tag">p · var(--font-body)</code>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="mono">Aa 0123 — confirms JetBrains Mono is actually loaded, not falling back to a system font.</p>
            <code class="atom-tag">.mono · var(--font-mono)</code>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3>Spacing</h3>
        <div class="scale-col">
          {spacingTokens.map((t) => (
            <div class="scale-row">
              <span class="scale-label">{t.name} = {t.value}</span>
              <span class="scale-bar" style={`width:${t.value}`}></span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <h3>Radius</h3>
        <div class="token-grid">
          {radiusTokens.map((t) => (
            <div class="token-swatch">
              <div class="radius-box" style={`border-radius:${t.value}`}></div>
              <div class="token-swatch-meta">
                <code class="token-swatch-name">{t.name}</code>
                <span class="token-swatch-hex">{t.value}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <h3>Shadow</h3>
        <div class="token-grid">
          {shadowTokens.map((t) => (
            <div class="token-swatch">
              <div class="shadow-demo-bg">
                <div class="shadow-box" style={`box-shadow:${t.value}`}></div>
              </div>
              <div class="token-swatch-meta">
                <code class="token-swatch-name">{t.name}</code>
                <span class="token-swatch-hex">{t.value}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="fine">
          Two elevation scales exist in parallel — tokens.css's <code>--shadow-*</code> and global.css's
          <code>--sh-1/2/3</code> — with different colour bases. Both are live; see the report.
        </p>

        <h3>Contrast reference</h3>
        <p class="lede">
          Sourced from {contrastSource}. {contrastRows.length} pairings checked, {contrastFailCount} failing.
        </p>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table class="contrast-table">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Pairing</th><th>Ratio</th><th>Required</th><th>Result</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {contrastRows.map((row) => (
                <tr>
                  <td>
                    <span class="contrast-swatch" style={`background:${row.bg}; color:${row.fg}`}>{row.label}</span>
                  </td>
                  <td class="mono">{row.ratio.toFixed(2)}:1</td>
                  <td class="mono">{row.required}:1</td>
                  <td class={row.pass ? "contrast-pass" : "contrast-fail"}>{row.pass ? "PASS" : "FAIL"}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-tint" id="atoms">
